This page is the table of contents of §49, 'Les groupes M_{ρ,σ} généraux', pp. 550–648 of the second part of Grothendieck's sequel to La Longue Marche, 'variations sur l'équation des lacets' (c. 1981–82). It contains no proofs, only headings with page numbers. What follows is my interpretation of the headings.

The setting. In §§46–48 (previous page) Grothendieck studies the 'relation des lacets'. This is the loop relation satisfied by automorphisms of the profinite fundamental group of P^1 minus {0,1,∞}, of the form αρ(α)^{-1} = βσ(β)^{-1}ε_1(μ−1). It is the cocycle or hexagon-type equation that later became part of the definition of the Grothendieck–Teichmüller group GT-hat. He builds from it a group scheme and groups M_{ρ,σ} attached to a pair (ρ,σ) inside Gl(2). The pair (ρ,σ) is probably the order-3 and order-2 generators of the modular group, PSL(2,Z) = Z/2 * Z/3; this reading is plausible but not certain.

What §49 does. It abstracts this construction to general data (item V.1, 'Données'), in a profinite context:
- a centralizer-type group Z_{ρ,σ} with a map δ_{ρ,σ};
- groups SoG_{ρ,σ} and G_{ρ,σ};
- centralizers and normalizers Z_ρ, Z_σ, N_ρ, N_σ and their variants N^*, SN^*;
- the groups SoM_{ρ,σ}, M_{ρ,σ}, Γ_{ρ,σ};
- groups Σ_{ρ,σ}, SG_{ρ,σ} and their #-variants;
- functoriality in the data.

The universal case. Item V.8 treats the universal case G* = Gl(2,Z)^ (profinite completion), with a subgroup Π_0. It studies two group extensions:
- SoΓ^!_{ρ,σ}, an extension of Z_{ρ,σ} = M[σ] by L_ρ × L_σ;
- So^ΠΓ^!_{ρ,σ}, an extension of Z_{ρ,σ} by μ = {±1}.
Item V.9 gives the structure of N_ρ^*, N_σ^* and a homomorphism M → M^G_{ρ,σ}/μ_G ↪ M_{ρ,σ}/μ_ρ. Here M is presumably the arithmetic group of automorphisms (M̃_{0,3}) mapping into the abstractly defined M_{ρ,σ}.

Other sections.
- Section II: a 'sans signes' version of the loop relation.
- Section III: properties of M̃_{0,3} = Ñ_{1,1}. This identifies the (0,3)-object with the once-punctured-torus object N_{1,1}, via Out(F_2) ≅ GL(2,Z), together with Gl(2,Z)^/±1.
- Section IV: bracketed scratch calculations fighting with the sign terms ε_2, ε_3.
- Section VI: recapitulates and refines the whole construction. Its last items, in the margin, cover the subgroups M_{ρ,σ}[ρ], M_{ρ,σ}[σ]; a return to the universal case; a digression giving a 'rectification' of the loop relation; and a 'lien avec 𝔾…' at p. 648.

Purpose. The section serves to understand the target of the Galois/GT-type action, M_{0,3} → M_{ρ,σ}(Z^), through an abstract group-theoretic construction depending only on (G,ρ,σ).
